                <pb facs="0171" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg65"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State Adee to Minister
                        Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-17"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(The minister is informed, relative to immigration to South Carolina, that the
                    advance of passage money to an alien does not violate the contract-labor law,
                    but that an alien must prove affirmatively that he will not become a public
                    charge and submit to examination as to other legal requirements.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
